# Records persistence, part 2 (run 860, agent-c; port/tools/modes-check.py's match check): a new
# process on the SRAM file match_race.input wrote (its Round-1 win time, name "AAA", is the
# Crystal Lake record).  The saved language pick skips the language menu, so START goes straight
# to the main menu; Time Attack on Crystal Lake: the race HUD's BEST TIME shows the saved record
# (1'19"16 at step ~1600; capture.sh -F 1600 -M).  The boot must not rewrite any chunk (a
# damaged chunk would be reset or restored from its mirror): the file stays byte-identical.
PADS 1
F 480:3 START          # title -> main menu (no language select)
F 600:3 DD             # Match Race -> Time Attack
F 680:3 A              # Time Attack
F 950:3 A              # rider
F 1050:3 A             # rider confirm
F 1150:3 A             # board
F 1300:3 A             # course: the first (Crystal Lake) -> race, BEST TIME on the HUD
# END 1650
